# COMPONENT

## Corpus

### PACKAGE

org.simplemodeling.textus.corpus

### DESCRIPTION

Textus Corpus manages immutable, versioned case collections. A corpus contains
reviewed inputs, deterministic fixture references, and expected evidence
references, but never provider, model, experiment arm, execution outcome, or
metric data.

# SERVICE

## CorpusRegistry

### DESCRIPTION

Publishes and resolves immutable corpus revisions and their cases. Textus AI
and Textus Experiment consume a revision by its id; they do not mutate it.

### OPERATION

#### publishCorpus

##### DESCRIPTION

Creates one immutable corpus revision. A later correction is published as a
new revision rather than changing a reviewed revision in place.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
PublishCorpus

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
PublishCorpusResult

##### IMPLEMENTATION
entity-create

##### ENTITY
CorpusRevision

#### registerCorpusCase

##### DESCRIPTION

Registers one reviewed case in a corpus revision. The case references sanitized
fixture and evidence resources; it does not embed credentials or raw provider
payloads.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
RegisterCorpusCase

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
RegisterCorpusCaseResult

##### IMPLEMENTATION
entity-create

##### ENTITY
CorpusCase

#### searchCorpusRevisions

##### DESCRIPTION

Finds published corpus revisions by stable corpus key, revision, or text.

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
SearchCorpusRevisions

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
SearchCorpusRevisionsResult

##### IMPLEMENTATION
entity-search

##### ENTITY
CorpusRevision

#### getCorpusRevision

##### DESCRIPTION

Gets one immutable corpus revision by its canonical entity id. This operation
is the component boundary used by consumers that retain a revision reference.

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
GetCorpusRevision

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
GetCorpusRevisionResult

#### getCorpusCase

##### DESCRIPTION

Gets one immutable corpus case by its canonical entity id. Consumers use the
returned revision id to verify that a case belongs to their fixed population.

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
GetCorpusCase

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
GetCorpusCaseResult

#### listCorpusCases

##### DESCRIPTION

Lists cases from one immutable corpus revision. Filters are only case metadata;
runtime profile and experiment selection remain outside this component.

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
ListCorpusCases

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
ListCorpusCasesResult

##### IMPLEMENTATION
entity-search

##### ENTITY
CorpusCase

# ENTITY

## CorpusRevision

### DESCRIPTION

One immutable, reviewable version of a named corpus.

### Attribute

| name        | type     | multiplicity |
|-------------+----------+--------------|
| id          | entityid | 1            |
| corpusKey   | CorpusKey | 1           |
| revision    | int      | 1            |
| name        | name     | 1            |
| kind        | CorpusKind | 1          |
| description | description | ?         |
| sourceDigest | CorpusSourceDigest | 1 |

## CorpusCase

### DESCRIPTION

A reviewed input case within exactly one corpus revision. References point to
sanitized resources whose content is resolved by the configured corpus store.

### Attribute

| name                      | type     | multiplicity |
|---------------------------+----------+--------------|
| id                        | entityid | 1            |
| corpusRevisionId          | entityid | 1            |
| caseKey                   | CorpusCaseKey | 1         |
| applicationPurpose        | ApplicationPurpose | 1    |
| difficulty                | CorpusDifficulty | ?       |
| fixtureReference          | CorpusFixtureReference | 1 |
| expectedEvidenceReference | CorpusEvidenceReference | ? |
| tags                      | CorpusTag | *           |

